And a second one to derive yourself: **(λx. λy. x)(λz. z)(λw. w)** — const applied to two identities. What should the final `Closure.body` be? (Work it out on paper first: const says "return my first argument." The first argument was `id`.) Assert it.

Note we test by *pattern-matching the value* and comparing bodies — we can't `assert_eq!` on `Value` (that's why no `PartialEq` derive). Real value comparison arrives with `quote` in 2c.

